  "partial_boundaries": [
    "Native bar y series currently Int64/Float64; category arrays Int64/Float64/Utf8/LargeUtf8/Boolean. Other native bar types return errors.",
    "Native options cover x/y, multiple series, horizontal, default/data-order sorting, side-by-side grouping and dimensions. Color rules, named-field sorting, other stack modes, labels, selection and advanced chart options are not claimed.",
    "Table RecordBatch input supports measured border/hide index/hide header/dimensions/alt. Existing Arrow metadata is preserved. Explicit virtual row numbers add truthful RangeIndex interoperability metadata for primitive types; complex-type implicit index metadata returns an error. Styler and arbitrary Python input coercion are not implemented.",
    "Empty/whitespace alt normalization and unmeasured data/parameter combinations remain unverified.",
    "Mixed Int64/Float64 integer magnitude beyond 2^53 returns an error; actual Python rounds in the separately captured large-int oracle. This is a known compatibility gap.",
    "Rust calls return Result<(), DataError>; no DeltaGenerator handle is exposed. Updates use existing session reruns."
  ],
  "usage": [
    "st.table(&batch)?;",
    "st.table(TableOptions::new(&batch).border(TableBorder::Horizontal).hide_index(false).width(480).height(220))?;",
    "st.bar_chart(&numeric_batch)?;",
    "st.bar_chart(BarChartOptions::native(&batch).x(\"group.name\").y(\"amount[0]\").horizontal(true).sort(false).height(260))?;"
  ],
